Bugfix: Stop the code integrity check from warning about an unsigned distribution

A fresh installation from a release archive showed "There were problems with the
code integrity check" and listed core plus every shipped app with
MissingSignatureException, "Signature data not found." Nothing an administrator
could do made it go away.

ownCloud.online does not sign its releases: there is no signature package and no
private key for the certificate the check verifies against, so the check could
never pass. The code already accounts for that - version.php declares the
unsigned channel 'bwtech', which turns the check off. The release build then
rewrote version.php to 'stable' and turned it back on, for exactly the artefacts
that ship to customers. The build now keeps the declared channel.

The update channel selector in the admin panel offered only ownCloud's channels,
so switching once armed the check permanently with no way back through the user
interface. 'bwtech' is now part of that list.

An instance that already carries the warning can clear it with
`occ config:app:delete core OC_Channel` (removes a channel override in the
database) or, if the channel has to stay on an ownCloud one, with
'integrity.check.disabled' => true in config.php.

